WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.234
-Former President Trump secretly
tested positive for COVID

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:06.834
before coming into contact
with more than 500 people,

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:09.100
including Joe Biden,
at their first debate.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.801
Meanwhile, Republicans
and Fox News

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:12.334
are suggesting a new variant

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:14.267
of the coronavirus
is a liberal hoax.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:16.934
For more on this,
it's time for A Closer Look.

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:21.300
♪♪

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.467
Despite receding to his hideout
in Mar-a-Lago,

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:27.200
where he's occasionally glimpsed
giving horrible toasts

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.567
on blurry cell phone footage

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:32.434
like a Florida swamp ghost
who haunts weddings.

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:35.067
Donald Trump remains under
multiple serious investigations.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.133
There's the investigation into
his election meddling

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.567
in Atlanta,
the investigation

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:39.834
of his business in New York,

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:41.601
and the congressional
investigation

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.701
of the insurrection
he stoked on January 6th.

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:46.534
Plus, I don't know, like,
a dozen other investigations

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:48.000
I've stopped
keeping track of.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.534
He's probably still got
a pending case

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:50.968
over the time he left
Air Force One

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:54.100
parked next to a fire hydrant
in Times Square.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.167
[Imitating Trump] Officer, I was
just running in real quick

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:58.234
to grab some M&amp;Ms
from the M&amp;M Store.

00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:01.067
We love -- We love M&amp;Ms,
don't we, folks?

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:02.667
We love them.

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.968
They've got your red one,
the nervous orange one.

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:06.634
and of course,
the sexy --

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:09.367
the sexy green M&amp;M.

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:13.868
Women want to be her and men --
men want to be with her.

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:18.501
I met her backstage
in '86, Jon Bovi concert.

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:22.334
I said, Jon Bovi.
I meant Bon Jovi.

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:25.334
I flubbed it.
I flubbed it.

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.267
You know, there's one thing
we know about the Donald --

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.033
I admit when I made a mistake.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.734
When I get it wrong,
I own up right away.

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:44.033
I met her at a Bon Jovi concert.

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:45.567
[Normally] And yet, even with
those various...

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:47.667
[laughing] investigations
intensifying,

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.801
Trump is still
freely confessing

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:51.467
to crimes
from past investigations.

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.501
Over the weekend,
he essentially confessed

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:55.067
to obstructing
the Russia investigation

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:57.033
by bragging about the fact
that he fired

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:59.634
then-FBI Director James Comey
to protect himself.

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:01.968
-Don't forget, I fired Comey.

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:03.734
Had I not fired Comey,

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:05.467
you might not be talking
to me right now

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:07.000
about a beautiful book

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.567
of 4 years
at the White House,

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:10.901
and we'll see
about the future.

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:13.567
The future's going
to be very interesting.

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:17.400
But I fired Comey --
that whole group --

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.834
and now that group
is coming back again?

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:24.334
I mean, it's not believable.

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:27.400
-He was definitely expecting
his interviewer

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:31.400
to jump in there
with a, "Good point, sir."

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.300
Trump always forgets that even
his most fervent supporters

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.801
sometimes can't follow
what he's talking about.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:39.501
I also like the Trump literally
starts a confession by saying,

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:40.968
"Don't forget."
He's like a defendant

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:42.100
jumping up in court, saying,

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.367
"Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Before you return

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:44.567
that murder weapon
to evidence,

00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:48.100
maybe, uh,
dust it for prints."

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.334
Trump supporters
always want to know

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:51.267
why people can't stop
talking about his crimes

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:53.467
when he can't stop talking
about his crimes.

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:55.367
In fact, Trump was so intent
on reminding everyone

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:58.234
he obstructed justice
during the Russia investigation

00:02:58.234 --> 00:03:00.200
that he again came back to it

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.200
later during the interview,
out of nowhere.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:06.634
-I was going to say before,
if I didn't fire Comey,

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:07.901
they were looking to take down

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:10.033
the President
of the United States

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:11.501
if I didn't fire him.

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:13.267
And some people said,

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:16.334
"He made a mistake
when he fired Comey."

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:19.534
And now those same people said
it was most incredible,

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:22.467
instinctual moves
that they've ever seen.

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:25.033
Because I wouldn't --
I might be here with you.

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:27.834
Perhaps we'll be talking
about something else.

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:32.934
But I don't think I could have
survived if I didn't fire him

00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:35.200
because it was like
a hornet's nest.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.334
When I fired him,
they all went crazy.

00:03:38.334 --> 00:03:41.367
-What are you talking about?

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:43.634
Even I don't ramble that much to
my therapist.

00:03:43.634 --> 00:03:45.434
I'm just kidding.
I don't have a therapist.

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:47.734
I have you guys.
A therapist --

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:49.033
A therapist would never...

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:52.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:55.234
I mean, it's cheaper.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:58.200
A therapist would never
put up with this many tangents.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.667
"I think, Seth,
it would just be more helpful

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:03.067
if we dug into your childhood."
Yeah, sure, sure, sure, sure.

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:06.534
But what if Al Pacino
had been in Dune?

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:10.434
Like what would...

00:04:12.467 --> 00:04:13.734
What would that even sound like?

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:15.934
[Imitating Al Pacino]
Alright, let's go.

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:20.834
The House of Atreides
will bring peace to Arrakis.

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.434
Oh, yeah.

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:27.434
[Normally] I genuinely wonder
if --

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:29.234
I genuinely wonder
if even Trump fans

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:31.033
are capable of understanding
what he's saying,

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:32.734
or if his stream
of consciousness rambling

00:04:32.734 --> 00:04:34.767
is just a soothing way
for them to fall asleep.

00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:37.067
Because I will say,
I would definitely listen to

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:39.267
one of those nature sound CDs
with Trump's voice

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:40.467
to help me doze off.

00:04:40.467 --> 00:04:41.667
[ Nature sounds play ]

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:42.901
-I never understood wind.

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:46.133
You know, I know windmills
very much.

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:48.133
They're noisy.

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:50.601
They kill the birds.

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:53.534
You want to see
a bird graveyard?

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:56.167
Go under a windmill someday.

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:58.133
You'll see more birds
than you've ever seen

00:04:58.133 --> 00:05:00.634
ever in your life.

00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:02.501
-Now, the congressional
investigation into Trump

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:03.868
for the January 6th insurrection

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:05.634
has been impeded,
in part by the fact

00:05:05.634 --> 00:05:07.767
that some of his cronies
have refused to cooperate,

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:09.534
like his former Chief of Staff,
Mark Meadows,

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:11.334
who cited executive privilege

00:05:11.334 --> 00:05:13.033
and said he would remain
loyal to Trump

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:14.701
and defy a congressional
subpoena,

00:05:14.701 --> 00:05:17.501
asking him to spill
any Trump secrets he might have.

00:05:17.501 --> 00:05:19.868
-Former Trump Chief of Staff
Mark Meadows,

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:22.567
who also happens to be
a former member of Congress,

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:24.000
he was a no show today,

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.067
despite the 1/6 committee's
demand

00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:28.267
that he appear
for a deposition,

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:29.534
10:00 AM sharp.

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:31.334
Meadows has also invoked

00:05:31.334 --> 00:05:33.901
Trump's claim
of executive privilege.

00:05:33.901 --> 00:05:36.400
-There you go. Mark Meadows
is claiming executive privilege.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.234
His interactions
with the president

00:05:38.234 --> 00:05:42.100
are private and confidential,
and as a loyal friend and ally,

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.534
he would never
betray that sacred --

00:05:43.534 --> 00:05:46.267
I'm sorry, what's that?
He wrote a book?

00:05:46.267 --> 00:05:47.534
Then he got
paid money for it.

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:49.200
Is it called
Home Gardening Tips,

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.434
But No Secrets
About Donald Trump?

00:05:50.434 --> 00:05:51.734
It's not?

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:53.100
Well, what's in it?
Juicy details

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.801
about all his private
interactions with Donald Trump?

00:05:54.801 --> 00:05:56.033
But what about
executive privilege?

00:05:56.033 --> 00:05:58.200
Alright, you know what?
I really feel like

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.067
you guys got to explain
this stuff to me

00:06:00.067 --> 00:06:01.033
before the show.

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:03.000
I mean,
even Wally's confused.

00:06:06.267 --> 00:06:09.300
Yeah.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.767
Yeah, you're right,
the clip packages

00:06:10.767 --> 00:06:12.634
always do a good job
of explaining stuff.

00:06:12.634 --> 00:06:13.901
The only problem
with the clip packages

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:16.400
is they never have
any Al Pacino.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.000
Alright.
Whatever, let's roll it.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.534
-Donald Trump tested positive
for coronavirus

00:06:21.534 --> 00:06:26.067
3 days before his first debate
against Joe Biden

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:28.267
on September 29th, 2020.

00:06:28.267 --> 00:06:30.667
This stunning revelation
is in a new book

00:06:30.667 --> 00:06:33.667
by former White House
Chief of Staff Mark Meadows

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:35.934
that was obtained by
The Guardian --

00:06:35.934 --> 00:06:39.767
a positive test the country
never knew about.

00:06:39.767 --> 00:06:42.801
Despite the positive test,
Trump attended an indoor event

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:45.234
with gold star
military families.

00:06:45.234 --> 00:06:47.801
Two days later,
on Tuesday, the 29th,

00:06:47.801 --> 00:06:51.434
Chris Wallace at Fox says Trump
was not tested at the debate

00:06:51.434 --> 00:06:54.334
because he arrived late
and they allowed him on stage

00:06:54.334 --> 00:06:57.200
because they were relying
on the honor system.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.400
Later that week,
on Thursday, the 1st,

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:01.868
Trump officially
tested positive,

00:07:01.868 --> 00:07:03.501
according to his doctor --

00:07:03.501 --> 00:07:04.968
-Who-ah.

00:07:07.334 --> 00:07:08.901
-Oh.

00:07:08.901 --> 00:07:10.467
First of all, I like
that Trump's aides

00:07:10.467 --> 00:07:12.567
won't talk to Congress,
but if they get a book deal,

00:07:12.567 --> 00:07:13.801
they'll tell the entire world

00:07:13.801 --> 00:07:15.634
the worst [bleep]
they can possibly think of.

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:18.834
"I'll never testify before
Congress about my good friend

00:07:18.834 --> 00:07:20.200
and loyal steward
Donald Trump,

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:23.868
a man I admire and look up to,
who I would never betray.

00:07:23.868 --> 00:07:27.033
You'll just have to read my book
titled Trash Can Human Being."

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.334
So it turns out,
Trump tested positive for COVID

00:07:30.334 --> 00:07:32.033
before a presidential debate
with Joe Biden

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:34.067
and kept it a secret.
Although in retrospect,

00:07:34.067 --> 00:07:37.000
I feel like maybe we should
have known from that debate

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.133
that he had something,
based on his performance.

00:07:39.133 --> 00:07:40.834
It was either COVID or rabies.

00:07:40.834 --> 00:07:42.367
-I'll ask Joe.
-[Stammering]

00:07:42.367 --> 00:07:44.801
-[Speaking incoherently]
-No! Hey, Mr. President.

00:07:44.801 --> 00:07:46.167
No, Mr. President.

00:07:46.167 --> 00:07:47.200
No, no. Go ahead.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.667
No, no, no, Mr. President.

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:50.033
-3 1/2 million, Joe.
-Mr. President --

00:07:50.033 --> 00:07:51.000
-Who-ah.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.067
-No, Mr. President.
-Go ahead.

00:07:52.067 --> 00:07:53.634
-Can I be honest?
It's a very important --

00:07:53.634 --> 00:07:55.200
-Try to be honest,
it'd be good for you.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:58.234
-He stood up --
-No.

00:07:58.234 --> 00:08:00.601
-Oh, good.
So not only did he have COVID,

00:08:00.601 --> 00:08:02.601
but his mouth was open
the entire time.

00:08:02.601 --> 00:08:04.701
It's like he was
trying to spread it.

00:08:04.701 --> 00:08:06.100
If you had a 4K TV,

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:08.334
you could actually see
the coronavirus particles

00:08:08.334 --> 00:08:10.634
coming out of his mouth.

00:08:10.634 --> 00:08:13.133
Trump secretly tested positive
for COVID, didn't tell anyone.

00:08:13.133 --> 00:08:15.200
And then he went to an event
with military families

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.367
and a presidential debate,

00:08:16.367 --> 00:08:17.767
knowing he was
potentially spreading COVID.

00:08:17.767 --> 00:08:19.300
In fact, The Washington Post
reported...

00:08:23.834 --> 00:08:26.667
He's like the Johnny Appleseed
of COVID.

00:08:26.667 --> 00:08:28.234
Now, people keep saying
that Trump looked terrible

00:08:28.234 --> 00:08:30.000
and we should have known
he had COVID.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.834
But I mean, when does he,
you know, not look terrible?

00:08:31.834 --> 00:08:34.567
I mean, look at this. Are we
supposed to be able to tell?

00:08:34.567 --> 00:08:36.133
I mean, look at these pictures.

00:08:36.133 --> 00:08:38.534
When was the COVID?

00:08:40.534 --> 00:08:43.467
He was never exactly
the picture of health, you know.

00:08:43.467 --> 00:08:45.167
You know how at the end
of pill commercials,

00:08:45.167 --> 00:08:47.167
they quickly list
all the possible side effects.

00:08:47.167 --> 00:08:51.634
They should just replace that
with a photo of Trump.

00:08:51.634 --> 00:08:53.234
He always looked like
a patient on "House"

00:08:53.234 --> 00:08:54.601
who gets saved
at the last minute

00:08:54.601 --> 00:08:56.167
by some unorthodox treatment.

00:08:56.167 --> 00:08:57.934
"Donald, there's only
one way to save you.

00:08:57.934 --> 00:08:59.834
We're gonna to hook you up --"
[ Laughs ] I'm sorry.

00:08:59.834 --> 00:09:02.601
Donald -- [ Laughs ]

00:09:02.601 --> 00:09:06.934
OK, OK. "Donald, there's
only one way to save you.

00:09:06.934 --> 00:09:08.934
We're going to hook up
your heart to a pig's heart

00:09:08.934 --> 00:09:12.467
and have you swap brains."

00:09:12.467 --> 00:09:15.234
Suffice it to say, it's a relief
to know he's no longer in charge

00:09:15.234 --> 00:09:17.868
as we face the prospect
once again of rising cases,

00:09:17.868 --> 00:09:19.701
a winter surge, and now,
a new,

00:09:19.701 --> 00:09:21.667
possibly even more transmissible
variant.

00:09:21.667 --> 00:09:24.501
Now, thankfully,
scientists, being the cautious,

00:09:24.501 --> 00:09:27.501
measured, people that they are,
have given it a totally benign

00:09:27.501 --> 00:09:30.334
and not at all terrifying name.

00:09:30.334 --> 00:09:32.367
[Echoing] The Omicron Variant.

00:09:32.367 --> 00:09:33.834
[ Lightning crashes ]

00:09:33.834 --> 00:09:36.834
[ Witch cackles ]

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.767
"The Omicron Variant"
sounds like a paperback

00:09:43.767 --> 00:09:44.934
I read at my grandma's house

00:09:44.934 --> 00:09:47.200
because there was
[bleep] else to do.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:50.000
No, Grandma, I don't want
to read your stories.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.501
What the [bleep[ is this?

00:09:52.501 --> 00:09:54.234
Seriously,
the Omicron variant?

00:09:54.234 --> 00:09:56.601
I thought scientists were
supposed to be mild-mannered,

00:09:56.601 --> 00:09:58.801
analytical types
who don't want you to panic.

00:09:58.801 --> 00:10:00.567
I get that they're just going
by the Greek alphabet,

00:10:00.567 --> 00:10:02.234
but the Greek alphabet
is very scary.

00:10:02.234 --> 00:10:03.868
I propose we start
naming the variants

00:10:03.868 --> 00:10:06.968
after popular child stars
of the '90s.

00:10:06.968 --> 00:10:09.000
I would just panic less
if Fauci was on TV,

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:12.267
telling us about
the Lipnicki variant.

00:10:12.267 --> 00:10:13.567
"You know, the Lipnicki variant,

00:10:13.567 --> 00:10:15.334
much like the actor
it's named after,

00:10:15.334 --> 00:10:17.601
it's infectious."

00:10:17.601 --> 00:10:20.267
Anyway, Omicron,
a.k.a. Haley Joel Omicron --

00:10:20.267 --> 00:10:22.267
see, it works --
is already here,

00:10:22.267 --> 00:10:24.467
and yet Republicans on Fox News
are dismissing it

00:10:24.467 --> 00:10:25.968
as some sort of liberal hoax,

00:10:25.968 --> 00:10:28.767
with one Republican calling it
"the midterm election variant,"

00:10:28.767 --> 00:10:30.767
another saying Joe Biden
wants to make COVID

00:10:30.767 --> 00:10:32.100
the forever pandemic,

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:33.601
and Fox News hosts suggesting

00:10:33.601 --> 00:10:36.434
Biden just came up with it
to help him politically.

00:10:36.434 --> 00:10:38.133
-The emergence of
the new COVID variant

00:10:38.133 --> 00:10:41.133
is sparking a fresh round
of conspiracy theories.

00:10:41.133 --> 00:10:43.434
Former White House doctor
turned MAGA congressman

00:10:43.434 --> 00:10:45.200
Ronny Jackson tweeted, quote,

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:49.434
"Here comes the MEV --
the Midterm Election Variant."

00:10:49.434 --> 00:10:51.801
-Democrats are already using
this to jam through

00:10:51.801 --> 00:10:55.133
their pro-lockdown,
anti-freedom agenda,

00:10:55.133 --> 00:10:57.167
but we're not surprised.
A new scary variant

00:10:57.167 --> 00:10:59.334
is another liberal cover up

00:10:59.334 --> 00:11:02.767
for Joe Biden's ongoing
and many failures.

00:11:02.767 --> 00:11:04.367
And maybe that might help them

00:11:04.367 --> 00:11:06.601
in the upcoming
midterm elections.

00:11:06.601 --> 00:11:08.334
-It's always a new variant.
-And you can always --

00:11:08.334 --> 00:11:11.300
you'll count on a variant about
every October, every 2 years.

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:12.601
-[ Laughs ]
-Oh, I think it's gonna -- Yep.

00:11:12.601 --> 00:11:14.133
You know,
you're probably right.

00:11:14.133 --> 00:11:16.534
-However...
-They could speed up.

00:11:16.534 --> 00:11:18.767
The variants
can come more quickly.

00:11:18.767 --> 00:11:21.234
-We're going to need
a new variant here.

00:11:21.234 --> 00:11:23.300
-Alright. First of all,
I hate to nitpick here,

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:26.100
but that's not how you mime
holding a phone.

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:27.701
See, if you're pretending
to hold a phone,

00:11:27.701 --> 00:11:29.734
you hold it like this.
Your hand isn't the phone.

00:11:29.734 --> 00:11:31.133
The phone is in your hand.

00:11:31.133 --> 00:11:33.100
Like, for example, if I were
to mime taking a phone call,

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:34.100
I would -- I would do this.

00:11:34.100 --> 00:11:36.267
"Hello? President of NBC?
Uh-huh.

00:11:36.267 --> 00:11:37.834
Yes, this is Seth Meyers.
[ Gasps ]

00:11:37.834 --> 00:11:41.834
I've used up my show's entire
tangent budget for the year?!

00:11:41.834 --> 00:11:43.767
Which year? 2022?!"

00:11:43.767 --> 00:11:46.033
Anyway, back to Fox News.

00:11:46.033 --> 00:11:47.334
Are you out of
your [bleep] mind?

00:11:47.334 --> 00:11:49.234
You think anyone wants
this pandemic to keep going?

00:11:49.234 --> 00:11:51.367
You think that's good
for Democrats politically?

00:11:51.367 --> 00:11:54.334
Everyone is miserable. No one
wants this thing to keep going.

00:11:54.334 --> 00:11:57.200
We all desperately want life
to go back to normal.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:58.701
I can't believe I'm saying this,

00:11:58.701 --> 00:12:01.033
but I give anything to be
on a packed "F" train

00:12:01.033 --> 00:12:04.601
high fiving rats
and reconnecting with the dude

00:12:04.601 --> 00:12:07.767
who insists on bringing his bike
on during rush hour.

00:12:07.767 --> 00:12:09.667
I miss that guy.

00:12:09.667 --> 00:12:11.200
Why do you have a bike
on the train, though?

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:13.968
Why are you bringing
one mode of transportation

00:12:13.968 --> 00:12:16.901
onto another,
slower mode of transport?

00:12:16.901 --> 00:12:20.901
Just ride the bike to work.
You'll beat us all there.

00:12:20.901 --> 00:12:23.567
We're all still dealing with
a once-in-a-century catastrophe

00:12:23.567 --> 00:12:25.267
that has resulted
in mass suffering,

00:12:25.267 --> 00:12:27.534
and we have one party
that either thinks it's a hoax

00:12:27.534 --> 00:12:30.133
or actively tries to spread it
to as many people as possible.

00:12:30.133 --> 00:12:32.567
We all desperately want
to get back to normal.

00:12:32.567 --> 00:12:35.000
The difference is,
one side is a bunch of proposals

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:36.067
for how to get there,

00:12:36.067 --> 00:12:37.501
and all the other side
can say is...

00:12:37.501 --> 00:12:38.934
-"Yabba-dabba-doo."

00:12:47.667 --> 00:12:51.434
